# Proposed by the swarm (2026-10-15); the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: the desk of 66-there-and-back-is-nothing.sim, as Arbor ships. The three have the display to themselves (F68): thirds of 517,
# of which Safari lacks 57. Finder and TextEdit lend it, each by what it can spare: Finder has 16 over its smallest size, TextEdit 277
# over the smallest size worth showing. A floating window's frame is its person's (F64): the Terminal is not touched.
# There and back is nothing all the same: everybody has the place and the size they had.
# Reference: T07, F61, F64, F68.
display-size 1600x900 31
open Finder 920x436 min 501x300
open Safari 1324x791 min 574x240
open TextEdit 673x439 min 115x100
open Terminal 877x499
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
dock 103 right
expect size 101 514x845
expect size 102 574x845
expect size 103 464x845
expect still 104
# ⌘H in Finder. The neighbours close up meanwhile.
focus 101
hide Finder
flush
expect hidden 101
expect still 104
unhide Finder
flush
expect visible 101
expect size 101 514x845
expect size 102 574x845
expect size 103 464x845
expect left-of 101 102
expect left-of 102 103
expect still 104
# ⌘M in Safari, and back out of the Dock.
minimize 102
expect hidden 102
restore 102
expect size 101 514x845
expect size 102 574x845
expect size 103 464x845
expect still 104
# Two of them, and the one that went first comes back first.
hide Finder
flush
minimize 102
unhide Finder
flush
restore 102
expect size 101 514x845
expect size 102 574x845
expect size 103 464x845
# Looking around meanwhile changes nothing: the view is not the arrangement.
minimize 103
zoom 102
show-all
restore 103
show-all
expect size 101 514x845
expect size 102 574x845
expect size 103 464x845
expect size 104 877x499
